# Copy this to .env and fill in real values. .env is gitignored -- never
# commit real secrets. Read by internal/envfile at process startup for
# every laforge-* service (cmd/laforge-api, -orchestrator, -gateway,
# -runner) when run directly (`go run ./cmd/laforge-api`); under
# docker-compose, compose's own env_file handling loads this file into
# each container instead, so the same .env serves both paths.
#
# See USAGE.md for exactly how to register a GitHub App and get the
# values below.

# --- database (all four services) ---
# Commented out on purpose: docker-compose sets this itself (api/gateway
# via `environment:`, which always wins over env_file for the same key;
# orchestrator/runner via an explicit -db-url flag), so this is inert
# under compose regardless. Uncomment and point it at your own real
# Postgres only if you're running a service directly on your host
# instead (`go run ./cmd/laforge-api`) -- the value below is just an
# example shape, not a value to keep as-is.
# DATABASE_URL=host=/tmp port=5432 user=<you> dbname=laforge_dev sslmode=disable

# --- laforge-api: GitHub App identity ---
# Required. The App's own webhook secret (set when you registered it).
GITHUB_APP_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# The App's user-to-server OAuth credentials (same App, not a second
# registration) -- required for real sign-in; without them
# /auth/github/login exists but the redirect it builds won't work.
GITHUB_APP_CLIENT_ID=
GITHUB_APP_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Optional, together: lets the server mint its own installation access
# tokens (internal/ghclient/app.go) instead of falling back to
# GITHUB_SERVICE_TOKEN for every repository's content-fetch. Both unset
# is a supported, real configuration -- everything falls back to
# GITHUB_SERVICE_TOKEN below.
GITHUB_APP_ID=
# A relative path like .dev-certs/your-app.private-key.pem resolves the
# same way whether laforge-api runs directly (go run, from the repo
# root) or under docker-compose (which bind-mounts ./.dev-certs to the
# api container's own working directory for exactly this reason) --
# keep the key there and this needs no per-environment adjustment.
GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY_PATH=
# Cosmetic only -- builds "Install on GitHub" links in the admin UI.
GITHUB_APP_SLUG=

# Optional. A personal access token (repo scope) or another service
# account's token -- posts LaForge's own commit-status checks back to
# GitHub, and is the fallback for verifying a repository's real clone
# URL when it has no installation behind it.
GITHUB_SERVICE_TOKEN=

# Comma-separated GitHub logins with instance-wide admin -- the only
# action that needs this is approving an installed repository into
# LaForge's own tracking (there's no repository yet to check
# repository_access against). Empty means nobody can approve anything
# yet, a safe default over silently allowing everyone.
LAFORGE_ADMIN_LOGINS=

# --- laforge-api: addressing ---
# LISTEN_ADDR isn't set here on purpose: laforge-api (default :8080) and
# laforge-gateway (default :8443) both read a var of this same name with
# different real defaults already built in, and this one .env is loaded
# by both -- setting it here would hand them the same port. Override it
# per service by exporting it inline instead, if you ever need to:
# LISTEN_ADDR=:8081 go run ./cmd/laforge-api
PUBLIC_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080
UI_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5173

# --- agent reach-back addresses (only when deploying to a real hoster) ---
# The addresses a DEPLOYED HOST connects back on -- NOT localhost, but an
# address instances on your hoster can route to (a LAN IP or a public
# hostname). Leave both empty to deploy without agents (the default,
# and what the fake builder uses). When you set GATEWAY_PUBLIC_ADDR to a
# non-localhost name, regenerate the gateway cert with GATEWAY_EXTRA_SANS so
# it matches (see scripts/gen-dev-certs.sh).
GATEWAY_PUBLIC_ADDR=
API_PUBLIC_URL=
# A real git checkout content can be loaded from -- see
# internal/api/server.go's RepoRoot doc comment for the single-checkout
# limitation this carries.
REPO_ROOT=.
# Only set to "true" when PUBLIC_BASE_URL and UI_BASE_URL above are
# genuinely different origins in production (not just different ports on
# localhost) and both serve real HTTPS -- see Server.CrossOriginCookies's
# own doc comment. Local dev and a same-registrable-domain split both
# leave this unset.
LAFORGE_CROSS_DOMAIN_COOKIES=

# --- laforge-gateway: mTLS ---
# Required. Generate real dev certs with scripts/gen-dev-certs.sh (see
# its own header comment) -- these are never meant to be committed.
GATEWAY_CA_CERT=.dev-certs/ca.crt
GATEWAY_SERVER_CERT=.dev-certs/server.crt
GATEWAY_SERVER_KEY=.dev-certs/server.key
